  "question": "If $$y=x^3+\\tan x,$$ find $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "<b>First derivative</b><br>$$\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+\\sec^2x.$$<br><b>Second differentiation</b><br>$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+2\\sec x(\\sec x\\tan x).$$<br>Therefore, $$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+2\\sec^2x\\tan x.$$",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+\\sec^2x$",
    "B": "$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=3x^2+2\\sec^2x\\tan x$",
    "C": "$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+2\\sec x\\tan x$",
    "D": "$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+2\\sec^2x\\tan x$"
